# Plan: 170-002-fix — P0-5 Docker Spawn Race Window Closure

## Problem
Sprint 169 Bug 2A: spawn-backend-docker.ts writes a prompt file BEFORE the .hb heartbeat
exists on disk. If _cleanupOrphanedPromptFiles() fires during this ~3s window (e.g. a
sibling worker calls kill()), getActiveWorkerIds() finds no .hb for the new worker → the
prompt gets DELETED → spawned worker fails immediately.

## Fix Strategy
Add an in-memory PENDING_SPAWNS Set to src/core/active-workers.ts:
- markPending(taskId): called in spawn() BEFORE prompt write
- markActive(taskId): called AFTER .hb written (heartbeat is now authoritative)
- clearPending(taskId): called on ALL error paths (spawn failure, image missing, etc.)
- getActiveWorkerIds returns union(PENDING_SPAWNS, fromHeartbeats) — deduped

Wire into spawn-backend-docker.ts:
- markPending at top of spawn() before acquireSpawnTimeLocks
- markActive after writeFileSync(hbPath) in runSpawn()
- clearPending in catch block of spawn() (covers all throw paths)
- clearPending in spawnOutcome.ok === false path (non-throw error return)

## Files to Change
1. src/core/active-workers.ts — add PENDING_SPAWNS Set + 5 new exported functions
2. src/orchestra/spawn-backend-docker.ts — import + wire markPending/markActive/clearPending

## Tests (already written — must go GREEN)
- tests/core/active-workers-pending.test.ts: 4 unit tests
- tests/orchestra/docker-spawn-race.test.ts: 2 integration tests
